WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.207 --> 00:00:00.927
- Hi

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:03.296
(laughing)
(upbeat music)

00:00:06.616 --> 00:00:08.074
So I spend most of my time

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:10.220
sitting in between these
two sleeve-less wonders.

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:11.986
The other day they got in a fight

00:00:11.986 --> 00:00:13.765
about whether beer pong

00:00:13.765 --> 00:00:15.299
or flip cup was better.

00:00:15.299 --> 00:00:17.000
I don't care, so I'm the moderator.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.136
But these guys are gonna have it out

00:00:19.136 --> 00:00:22.210
to decide what's a better drinking game:

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:24.123
Beer Pong or Flip Cup

00:00:24.235 --> 00:00:27.363
I'll let them give you
their drinking credentials.

00:00:27.363 --> 00:00:28.305
- Ladies first.

00:00:28.305 --> 00:00:28.964
- Oh thanks.

00:00:28.964 --> 00:00:30.243
My name's Jordan.

00:00:30.243 --> 00:00:31.341
I like to drink.

00:00:31.341 --> 00:00:32.575
I like to have fun.

00:00:32.575 --> 00:00:33.203
I'm not really sure what other kind

00:00:33.203 --> 00:00:34.178
of credentials I need.

00:00:34.658 --> 00:00:35.420
- I'm Ryan.

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:37.673
Chapman University 2013.

00:00:37.673 --> 00:00:38.615
Was in a fraternity,

00:00:38.615 --> 00:00:40.006
so I definitely know a little bit

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:41.285
about drinking games.

00:00:41.285 --> 00:00:42.026
Probably more than her,

00:00:42.026 --> 00:00:44.606
but that remains to be seen.

00:00:44.606 --> 00:00:46.113
- So these guys both did a little research

00:00:46.113 --> 00:00:47.390
and talked to a lot of people

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:49.480
to try and make a defense and a case

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:52.545
for their game of choice.

00:00:52.905 --> 00:00:54.402
They're going to show
each other the footage,

00:00:54.832 --> 00:00:56.508
they're going to show me the footage,

00:00:56.508 --> 00:00:59.063
and we're going to let the viewers at home

00:00:59.063 --> 00:01:01.158
decide who's in the right.

00:01:01.158 --> 00:01:02.461
But before we do that,

00:01:02.461 --> 00:01:04.791
we have to figure out who gets to go first

00:01:04.791 --> 00:01:05.501
and we're going to do that

00:01:05.501 --> 00:01:07.728
through a quick game of eye-to-eye.

00:01:07.728 --> 00:01:08.194
- Let's do it.

00:01:08.904 --> 00:01:09.717
- Alright.

00:01:09.717 --> 00:01:11.424
- So quick disclaimer from Jordan.

00:01:11.424 --> 00:01:13.354
- We realize that we're
breaking the elbow rule,

00:01:13.354 --> 00:01:14.916
but we don't have enough space,

00:01:14.916 --> 00:01:15.864
so get over it.

00:01:15.864 --> 00:01:17.691
- Three. Two. One.

00:01:18.681 --> 00:01:19.107
(beep)

00:01:19.107 --> 00:01:20.238
Well that was great.

00:01:20.238 --> 00:01:21.620
- You're both terrible at this.

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:23.545
Three. Two. One.

00:01:25.085 --> 00:01:26.416
- Let's go. Me first.

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:28.162
- Alright, Ryan. Cue it up.

00:01:28.162 --> 00:01:29.491
- Your desktop is a mess, dude.

00:01:29.491 --> 00:01:31.302
How are you going to have
an organized argument

00:01:31.302 --> 00:01:32.947
if you can't even have
an organized computer?

00:01:32.947 --> 00:01:34.591
- Oh I'll show you how I
have an organized argument--

00:01:34.591 --> 00:01:35.713
just give me a second for it to load

00:01:35.713 --> 00:01:36.793
and then I'll show you.

00:01:37.323 --> 00:01:39.185
(dramatic acoustic music)

00:01:39.475 --> 00:01:40.404
Beer Pong.

00:01:40.404 --> 00:01:42.528
The undeniable poster-child
of drinking games.

00:01:42.528 --> 00:01:44.026
And today, I'm going to prove to you

00:01:44.026 --> 00:01:46.257
why beer pong is the
greatest drinking game

00:01:46.257 --> 00:01:47.000
in the world.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:47.788
But, if I'm right,

00:01:48.978 --> 00:01:50.338
and I'm definitely right,

00:01:50.338 --> 00:01:51.456
you probably already knew that.

00:01:52.286 --> 00:01:53.012
So to start my case,

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:54.725
I took to the streets of LA

00:01:54.725 --> 00:01:56.379
to ask what was the best drinking game.

00:01:57.049 --> 00:01:59.026
Keep in mind, these people have no idea

00:01:59.026 --> 00:02:00.674
I'm making a video about beer pong.

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:03.694
In your opinion, what is
the best beer drinking game?

00:02:03.694 --> 00:02:05.318
- The best beer drinking
game, for sure, is beer pong.

00:02:05.888 --> 00:02:07.454
- Beer pong, it's more social.

00:02:07.834 --> 00:02:08.569
- King's cup.

00:02:08.569 --> 00:02:09.335
- Beer pong.

00:02:09.335 --> 00:02:09.730
- Beer pong.

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:10.062
- Beer pong.

00:02:10.062 --> 00:02:10.473
- Kings.

00:02:10.473 --> 00:02:11.587
- Beer pong.

00:02:11.587 --> 00:02:12.027
- Beer pong.

00:02:12.027 --> 00:02:13.230
- This game we call "Things".

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:14.310
- Is that even a game?

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:15.076
- Recap.

00:02:15.076 --> 00:02:18.155
That's one, two, three, four, five,

00:02:18.155 --> 00:02:20.271
six, seven, eight votes for beer pong,

00:02:20.271 --> 00:02:23.313
and one, two votes for King's cup,

00:02:23.313 --> 00:02:26.401
and also one vote for
some game called "Things".

00:02:26.401 --> 00:02:29.489
Yes, that means a game that
I've never even heard of

00:02:29.489 --> 00:02:31.275
got more votes than flip cup.

00:02:31.275 --> 00:02:33.181
Which put up a big, fat donut.

00:02:33.181 --> 00:02:34.873
You get it. Moving on.

00:02:34.873 --> 00:02:36.339
I could show you how fun beer pong is

00:02:36.339 --> 00:02:38.742
by showing you clips like
this epic beer pong dunk

00:02:38.742 --> 00:02:40.179
from my college days.

00:02:40.439 --> 00:02:42.224
(people screaming)

00:02:42.224 --> 00:02:42.844
Shit's epic.

00:02:42.844 --> 00:02:44.039
- That has nothing to do with beer pong,

00:02:44.039 --> 00:02:45.937
he just belly-flopped onto a table.

00:02:47.047 --> 00:02:48.488
- But instead, I'm just going to show you

00:02:48.488 --> 00:02:50.247
me and my dad, chillin' over a game of BP

00:02:50.247 --> 00:02:51.060
in the backyard.

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:52.165
- Does anyone in your family

00:02:52.165 --> 00:02:53.972
have sleeves on their shirts, Ryan?

00:02:54.842 --> 00:02:55.297
- Alright.

00:02:57.277 --> 00:02:58.451
- Not bad for an old dude.

00:02:58.451 --> 00:02:59.457
- Yeah, whatever.

00:02:59.457 --> 00:03:00.781
(laughs)

00:03:00.781 --> 00:03:02.522
You've seen this game before,

00:03:02.522 --> 00:03:03.945
and you saw it for the first time,

00:03:03.945 --> 00:03:05.714
one summer night, actually in this house,

00:03:05.714 --> 00:03:06.854
when we were having a party.

00:03:06.854 --> 00:03:07.664
- Right.

00:03:08.064 --> 00:03:09.716
- What did you think of
when you first saw it?

00:03:09.716 --> 00:03:11.538
- I think that night,

00:03:11.538 --> 00:03:13.318
one of your uncles was over here,

00:03:13.318 --> 00:03:15.482
who's about my age, and we figured,

00:03:15.482 --> 00:03:17.284
you know what, that looks like a game

00:03:17.284 --> 00:03:20.021
that we could proudly
school these young kids on.

00:03:20.021 --> 00:03:22.592
I was never really into
chugging games and I figured,

00:03:22.592 --> 00:03:24.301
well, why not play a skill game,

00:03:24.301 --> 00:03:26.560
while having a casual sip of your beer?

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:29.414
I mean the two just
went together naturally.

00:03:29.414 --> 00:03:32.572
And I believe we actually did
beat you guys all that night,

00:03:32.572 --> 00:03:33.849
and you weren't too happy about it.

00:03:33.849 --> 00:03:35.080
- You lost the first game
from my recollection.

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:36.473
- Okay, is that what it was?

00:03:37.043 --> 00:03:39.180
I don't think there is,
like, an age requirement,

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:41.200
or anything like that,

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:42.720
pretty much anybody can play.

00:03:44.570 --> 00:03:46.834
- Aw man, see that form dad?

00:03:47.414 --> 00:03:48.929
(laughs)

00:03:51.679 --> 00:03:52.739
So to close this thing out,

00:03:52.739 --> 00:03:54.084
I sent an e-mail to the entire office

00:03:54.084 --> 00:03:55.941
to see who would like to participate

00:03:55.941 --> 00:03:57.311
in a beer pong tournament.

00:03:57.311 --> 00:03:59.981
Within one hour, I had 60 volunteers.

00:04:00.581 --> 00:04:02.350
But, due to time, I had to cut it down

00:04:02.350 --> 00:04:03.580
to an 18 tournament.

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:05.438
(techno music)

00:04:15.538 --> 00:04:16.573
Alright, let's be honest.

00:04:16.573 --> 00:04:18.245
Nobody wants to watch the qualifiers,

00:04:18.245 --> 00:04:19.666
so let's just skip to the finals.

00:04:20.816 --> 00:04:24.323
(dramatic music)

00:04:26.453 --> 00:04:27.019
- I will.

00:04:29.579 --> 00:04:30.324
- Balls back!

00:04:30.324 --> 00:04:30.882
- Alright.

00:04:32.152 --> 00:04:33.128
- You go girl.

00:04:33.658 --> 00:04:35.688
- Watch Malory with her elbows, though!

00:04:35.688 --> 00:04:36.353
- Nice.

00:04:37.543 --> 00:04:38.023
- Yeah!

00:04:38.023 --> 00:04:38.492
- Okay, okay.

00:04:38.492 --> 00:04:39.142
- Yeah!

00:04:40.522 --> 00:04:41.104
- You got it girl.

00:04:41.354 --> 00:04:43.854
- Where are you going
every time for defense?

00:04:45.334 --> 00:04:45.900
- Yeah, baby!

00:04:46.370 --> 00:04:47.371
- See what happened?

00:04:47.631 --> 00:04:49.105
- Well Kelsey's carrying your team.

00:04:52.085 --> 00:04:53.248
- You got to get this one, man.

00:04:53.428 --> 00:04:54.759
- Okay. That's a lot of pressure.

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:57.181
Oh!
- [Kelsey] You're there!

00:04:58.231 --> 00:04:59.162
- Yeah baby!

00:05:01.522 --> 00:05:02.761
- What am I doing?

00:05:03.892 --> 00:05:05.661
- Yeah, T-Lo!

00:05:05.811 --> 00:05:07.402
- We're falling apart.
We're falling apart.

00:05:09.762 --> 00:05:10.609
- Finally!

00:05:11.059 --> 00:05:11.825
Get that cup.

00:05:13.475 --> 00:05:14.197
- That's how we do.

00:05:15.667 --> 00:05:16.556
- No, please stop.

00:05:16.556 --> 00:05:17.200
- Look at T-Lo.

00:05:17.720 --> 00:05:18.684
- Oh!

00:05:20.364 --> 00:05:21.034
- Yes!

00:05:21.524 --> 00:05:23.289
- Hold on, I have a speech to make.

00:05:23.949 --> 00:05:25.288
This has been a good game.

00:05:25.288 --> 00:05:27.102
- Oh my god, stop--

00:05:27.102 --> 00:05:29.099
- I really enjoyed this game.

00:05:29.939 --> 00:05:31.165
- Okay. Winning an Oscar.

00:05:34.325 --> 00:05:36.113
- Oh wait, rebuttal right?

00:05:36.113 --> 00:05:37.713
- No rebuttal, it's the same front cup.

00:05:38.123 --> 00:05:39.321
- Fucking horseshit.

00:05:40.931 --> 00:05:42.207
- So what did we learn here today?

00:05:42.207 --> 00:05:43.216
Beer pong is the crowd favorite.

00:05:43.546 --> 00:05:45.236
It can be chill, or it can be crazy.

00:05:45.606 --> 00:05:47.674
It can be enjoyed by people young and old

00:05:47.674 --> 00:05:50.408
and it also lends itself
to decorum and competition,

00:05:50.408 --> 00:05:51.872
i.e. the tournament that we just had.

00:05:52.262 --> 00:05:53.822
And I guess that's my
favorite part about it,

00:05:53.822 --> 00:05:56.276
the competitive aspect that
it brings out in people,

00:05:56.276 --> 00:05:57.888
because when you step up to the table,

00:05:57.888 --> 00:05:59.116
you would swear that you could beat

00:05:59.116 --> 00:05:59.975
the people across from you,

00:05:59.975 --> 00:06:00.973
no matter who they are,

00:06:00.973 --> 00:06:02.413
and no matter how skilled you are.

00:06:04.893 --> 00:06:06.659
I didn't make that did I?

00:06:06.659 --> 00:06:07.243
- Almost.

00:06:07.243 --> 00:06:08.195
- That's fine.

00:06:08.195 --> 00:06:10.749
- So beer pong is the most popular,

00:06:10.749 --> 00:06:11.538
and that makes it the best?

00:06:12.018 --> 00:06:12.838
- Do you know how many people

00:06:12.838 --> 00:06:14.208
are going to think of
the first drinking game

00:06:14.208 --> 00:06:15.741
that comes to mind, and
just say that though?

00:06:16.071 --> 00:06:17.180
They are clearly not well-educated

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:18.759
in the art of drinking games.

00:06:18.759 --> 00:06:20.036
- Keep in mind, I asked 12 people

00:06:20.036 --> 00:06:21.104
and not one of them said flip cup.

00:06:21.104 --> 00:06:22.289
- Yeah, well. Just wait.

00:06:22.289 --> 00:06:25.516
- We do agree that just,
sheer logistics, flip cup

00:06:25.516 --> 00:06:27.166
is a simpler game for set up.

00:06:27.266 --> 00:06:28.488
- Flip cup is perhaps a little bit more

00:06:28.488 --> 00:06:29.719
logistically sound to set up,

00:06:29.719 --> 00:06:31.621
however, I still think that it's more

00:06:31.621 --> 00:06:33.178
just like savage and crazy.

00:06:33.178 --> 00:06:34.595
If you went to a family reunion and said

00:06:34.595 --> 00:06:36.406
"Hey, let's play this chugging game"

00:06:36.406 --> 00:06:37.706
I don't think everybody would be on board.

00:06:37.706 --> 00:06:39.703
- You're chugging like an ounce at a time

00:06:39.703 --> 00:06:41.607
and if you really don't
want to be in the game,

00:06:41.607 --> 00:06:42.791
you can be out the first round

00:06:42.791 --> 00:06:45.436
and have only drank one ounce of beer.
[Ryan] - Well that sounds like a good game

00:06:45.436 --> 00:06:47.141
when I don't want to play
anymore, I just leave.

00:06:47.141 --> 00:06:48.503
- Which game do you
think takes more skill?

00:06:48.853 --> 00:06:49.625
- Beer Pong.
[Jordan] - Beer pong.

00:06:49.625 --> 00:06:50.298
- I think beer pong.

00:06:50.298 --> 00:06:51.129
- Of course beer pong.

00:06:51.129 --> 00:06:52.611
But that's why it's not
the best drinking game,

00:06:52.611 --> 00:06:54.243
because it takes skill to have fun.

00:06:54.243 --> 00:06:56.180
- You're saying that
flip cup's a better game

00:06:56.180 --> 00:06:57.280
because anybody can play.

00:06:57.280 --> 00:06:57.720
- Right.

00:06:57.720 --> 00:06:58.533
- But that's not true.

00:06:58.533 --> 00:06:59.873
- I think it is true.

00:06:59.873 --> 00:07:00.855
- I think that somebody could step in

00:07:00.855 --> 00:07:02.944
and play beer pong and have a better time

00:07:02.944 --> 00:07:04.965
if they weren't, like,
into just craziness.

00:07:05.415 --> 00:07:06.706
- You know what? Let's go to my argument.

00:07:06.996 --> 00:07:08.796
And I'll stop using my words

00:07:09.196 --> 00:07:10.468
and just show you what I mean.

00:07:10.468 --> 00:07:11.536
- Are we ready for this?

00:07:11.536 --> 00:07:12.511
- Yeah.

00:07:13.091 --> 00:07:13.813
- Drinking games.

00:07:13.813 --> 00:07:15.887
We've all probably played our fair share,

00:07:15.887 --> 00:07:18.270
and beer pong is arguably
the most popular, right?

00:07:19.110 --> 00:07:20.396
But is it the best?

00:07:20.646 --> 00:07:21.704
I sure don't think so.

00:07:22.064 --> 00:07:24.154
In fact, I think beer pong is stupid.

00:07:24.864 --> 00:07:25.607
- That's a good point.

00:07:25.607 --> 00:07:27.023
- [Jordan] You've got some friends over

00:07:27.023 --> 00:07:28.881
and you decide to play
some drinking games.

00:07:29.281 --> 00:07:30.158
You could play beer pong.

00:07:30.158 --> 00:07:32.309
Only half the room will
get to play at a time,

00:07:32.309 --> 00:07:33.524
and it takes what seems like forever

00:07:33.524 --> 00:07:35.266
to finish one low energy,

00:07:35.266 --> 00:07:36.218
boring game.

00:07:36.218 --> 00:07:38.656
- That's a lot of adjectives
here. Not a lot of facts.

00:07:38.656 --> 00:07:40.049
- [Jordan] Or you could play flip cup!

00:07:40.419 --> 00:07:41.722
Everyone gets to be involved,

00:07:41.722 --> 00:07:42.626
the energy is amped up,

00:07:42.626 --> 00:07:44.043
and you're having a blast.

00:07:44.643 --> 00:07:46.051
Which one sounds more appealing?

00:07:47.451 --> 00:07:48.190
Think I'm wrong?

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:49.615
Let's see what the
people of LA have to say.

00:07:49.615 --> 00:07:51.426
Beer pong or flip cup, which is better?

00:07:52.176 --> 00:07:52.678
- Flip cup.

00:07:52.678 --> 00:07:53.847
- I love flip cup better, yeah.

00:07:54.157 --> 00:07:55.844
- Would you pick beer pong over flip cup?

00:07:56.254 --> 00:07:57.951
- No, I like flip cup.
[Jordan] - You pick flip cup?

00:07:57.951 --> 00:07:59.251
- I'm gonna say beer pong.

00:07:59.251 --> 00:08:00.226
- Flip cup, I would say.

00:08:00.466 --> 00:08:01.510
- I like flip cup.

00:08:02.450 --> 00:08:04.129
- I'm better at beer pong,
so I'll say beer pong.

00:08:04.129 --> 00:08:08.643
- In theory, I would
say, you know, beer pong.

00:08:08.643 --> 00:08:09.914
In practice...

00:08:09.914 --> 00:08:10.481
flip cup.

00:08:10.481 --> 00:08:10.971
- Why?

00:08:10.971 --> 00:08:13.374
- It's more intense, there's more people,

00:08:13.374 --> 00:08:14.522
it's more involved.

00:08:14.522 --> 00:08:16.987
- I think that you can really

00:08:18.267 --> 00:08:19.573
yell a lot more in flip cup.

00:08:19.573 --> 00:08:20.838
- Do you think that's more exciting than

00:08:20.838 --> 00:08:22.176
just just shooting a
ping-pong ball into a cup?

00:08:22.176 --> 00:08:22.803
- It is. It's a rush.

00:08:22.803 --> 00:08:24.381
It's all that pressure going into it,

00:08:24.381 --> 00:08:25.194
that's why.

00:08:25.194 --> 00:08:26.146
- What do you have to say to that?

00:08:26.146 --> 00:08:27.795
- I think, well, I think there's...

00:08:27.795 --> 00:08:30.070
I don't know. There's
more competitiveness,

00:08:30.070 --> 00:08:31.579
like, with beer pong...

00:08:31.579 --> 00:08:33.739
- So the people of LA chose flip cup,

00:08:33.739 --> 00:08:35.665
but do you still think beer pong

00:08:35.665 --> 00:08:36.525
is the best drinking game?

00:08:37.225 --> 00:08:38.847
Well we took two people
from Ryan's tournament,

00:08:38.847 --> 00:08:40.704
and decided to see what they had to say

00:08:40.704 --> 00:08:41.540
about the debate.

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:47.326
- Yes.

00:08:50.363 --> 00:08:51.037
Oh man.

00:08:51.037 --> 00:08:51.710
- Oh.

00:08:51.710 --> 00:08:52.964
Down. Up. Down.
[Bald Man] Down. Up. Down.

00:08:52.964 --> 00:08:55.797
- Flip cup. The game is over pretty fast.

00:08:55.797 --> 00:08:57.213
I can get games in.

00:08:57.213 --> 00:08:58.862
And a lot of people can play,

00:08:58.862 --> 00:09:01.597
there's, like, no limit to how many people

00:09:01.597 --> 00:09:02.805
can play in a game,

00:09:02.805 --> 00:09:03.849
so that's really fun.

00:09:03.849 --> 00:09:04.848
And it's teamwork.

00:09:05.158 --> 00:09:06.823
- You got it, you got it.

00:09:06.823 --> 00:09:08.029
- It gets everyone involved,

00:09:08.029 --> 00:09:09.747
that's what's fun about flip cup.

00:09:10.357 --> 00:09:11.883
- If you have a large group of people,

00:09:11.883 --> 00:09:13.555
flip cup is more fun to play.

00:09:13.555 --> 00:09:14.275
- It's really fun.

00:09:15.505 --> 00:09:16.108
- Nice!

00:09:18.678 --> 00:09:20.613
- So, what did we learn?

00:09:20.613 --> 00:09:23.277
Well, the people who
like beer pong the best

00:09:23.277 --> 00:09:25.040
are mostly just the
ones who are good at it.

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:27.581
Which doesn't make it
the best drinking game,

00:09:27.581 --> 00:09:28.996
it just makes it the best drinking game

00:09:28.996 --> 00:09:31.898
for sore losers with good
hand-eye coordination.

00:09:31.898 --> 00:09:32.943
- What?

00:09:32.943 --> 00:09:33.755
- Wow!

00:09:33.755 --> 00:09:34.916
- What are you talking about?

00:09:34.916 --> 00:09:36.077
- Mic drop.

00:09:36.077 --> 00:09:37.331
- The only point you made was that

00:09:37.331 --> 00:09:38.794
more people could play with flip cup,

00:09:38.794 --> 00:09:40.466
which is, like, not even necessarily true.

00:09:40.466 --> 00:09:41.952
- Did you see all the
people on the street?

00:09:41.952 --> 00:09:43.879
It was six to three.

00:09:43.879 --> 00:09:45.202
The more people you get involved,

00:09:45.202 --> 00:09:46.015
the more fun it is.

00:09:46.015 --> 00:09:47.199
It's a more high energy game,

00:09:47.199 --> 00:09:48.174
you're not just sitting there

00:09:48.174 --> 00:09:49.057
throwing a ping-pong ball

00:09:49.057 --> 00:09:50.218
at a bunch of red cups.

00:09:50.218 --> 00:09:51.773
- What parties have you been to

00:09:51.773 --> 00:09:53.236
where beer pong is not high energy?

00:09:53.236 --> 00:09:54.838
- I'm not even trying to say that flip cup

00:09:54.838 --> 00:09:55.906
is the best drinking game,

00:09:55.906 --> 00:09:57.671
because I don't necessarily
believe that either,

00:09:57.671 --> 00:09:59.227
I just think it's better than beer pong.

00:09:59.757 --> 00:10:00.813
- Don't agree.

00:10:00.813 --> 00:10:02.756
- All you had to say is
"beer pong is popular" and

00:10:02.756 --> 00:10:04.196
"people can be good at it".

00:10:04.196 --> 00:10:05.426
- I didn't say beer pong was popular,

00:10:05.426 --> 00:10:06.517
I said beer pong was the best.

00:10:06.517 --> 00:10:08.189
- And then I asked people
if they'd pick flip cup

00:10:08.189 --> 00:10:09.234
over beer pong...

00:10:09.234 --> 00:10:11.533
- Yeah, you had to mention
the name "Flip cup" to them.

00:10:11.533 --> 00:10:13.672
- That doesn't matter,
everybody picked flip cup.

00:10:13.672 --> 00:10:14.824
- She's pulling a lot of muscle over here

00:10:14.824 --> 00:10:15.600
with these stretches.

00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:17.220
- I don't think I'm stretching anything.

00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:18.334
Let me ask you this:

00:10:18.334 --> 00:10:20.376
What's the point of drinking games?

00:10:20.376 --> 00:10:21.710
- One, to socialize.

00:10:21.710 --> 00:10:22.940
Or two, to get drunk.

00:10:22.940 --> 00:10:24.971
- Great. So fip cup does
both of those things

00:10:24.971 --> 00:10:25.608
- Does it though?

00:10:25.608 --> 00:10:27.181
- Beer pong does one of those things.

00:10:27.181 --> 00:10:28.241
- Beer pong does both of those things.

00:10:28.241 --> 00:10:29.967
- I have never gotten drunk
during a game of beer pong.

00:10:29.967 --> 00:10:30.826
It's too slow.

00:10:30.826 --> 00:10:31.987
- It takes too long.

00:10:31.987 --> 00:10:33.055
- Who are you guy playing against?

00:10:33.055 --> 00:10:35.089
You're playing a 35 minute beer pong game,

00:10:35.089 --> 00:10:36.375
maybe you should just not be playing

00:10:36.375 --> 00:10:37.452
drinking games in general.

00:10:37.452 --> 00:10:38.017
- Or maybe you shouldn't--

00:10:38.017 --> 00:10:39.162
- Alright, alright, alright.

00:10:39.162 --> 00:10:40.892
Let's wrap this up. Let's wrap this up.

00:10:40.892 --> 00:10:42.304
So I think you both have presented

00:10:42.304 --> 00:10:43.925
some pretty valid arguments here.

00:10:43.925 --> 00:10:45.282
On Jordan's side, she's
saying that flip cup

00:10:45.282 --> 00:10:46.835
is a more inclusive game,

00:10:46.835 --> 00:10:48.457
that it doesn't require as much skill,

00:10:48.457 --> 00:10:50.060
has more people, gets you more drunk,

00:10:50.060 --> 00:10:50.875
ends a little more rowdy.

00:10:50.875 --> 00:10:53.551
Ryan also presents a valuable argument,

00:10:53.551 --> 00:10:56.336
which is that there's
sort of a team aspect

00:10:56.336 --> 00:10:59.009
to beer pong, people can get dolled-up,

00:10:59.009 --> 00:10:59.978
make their uniforms.

00:10:59.978 --> 00:11:02.089
There's a lot of flexibility in beer pong

00:11:02.089 --> 00:11:04.854
as to whether it's a rowdy, fratty game,

00:11:04.854 --> 00:11:06.827
or whether it's just a casual, backyard,

00:11:06.827 --> 00:11:07.864
hang out kind of vibe.

00:11:07.864 --> 00:11:10.283
I feel like you both have
some pretty valid arguments.

00:11:10.283 --> 00:11:11.680
I don't know if I am qualified

00:11:11.680 --> 00:11:13.004
to really make this decision,

00:11:13.004 --> 00:11:14.536
so I think we need to throw this

00:11:14.536 --> 00:11:15.733
to the viewers at home.

00:11:15.733 --> 00:11:16.742
- It's all up to you guys.

00:11:17.152 --> 00:11:18.547
Make the right choice.

00:11:18.547 --> 00:11:22.495
(upbeat rock music)

